While verifying the duplicate-tag fix I drew two routes and found
neither had produced its duct run. Every fiber route in the Beltside
project from R-012 onward (2026-09-13) has no conduit run — R-001 to
R-011 do.

Cause: conduit_runs and conduit_structures are inserted with a
placeholder organization_id, exactly as fiber_routes and fiber_nodes
are, relying on a BEFORE INSERT trigger to resolve it from the project.
fiber_routes and fiber_nodes have that trigger; the two conduit tables
never got it. So the placeholder hit the organization_id foreign key
and the insert was rejected every time.

- migration: adds set_fiber_organization_id_from_project as a BEFORE
  INSERT trigger on conduit_runs and conduit_structures, the same one
  the fiber tables use. Verified by inserting with the placeholder and
  watching the real organization_id come back.
- The mirror failure was console.error only, which is exactly why this
  went unnoticed for a day of work. createFiberRoute and createFiberNode
  now return a warning, and the map surfaces it instead of reporting a
  clean success over a half-finished write. The route/node itself still
  saves — losing the drawing would be the worse outcome.

Not included: backfilling the duct runs missing for R-012, R-013 and
R-014. That changes what the Ductería module shows on a live project,
so it is Marcelo's call.

